tedModelBehavior cause chain)'","E6(f): a proving command that passes on a substitute which bypasses the new behavior does not prove the criterion"],"finding":"The load-bearing assumption — that a pydantic-ai 1.107.x VALIDATION exhaustion yields UnexpectedModelBehavior.__cause__ -> ToolRetryError -> ModelRetry.__cause__ carrying the identical Rebar object — is an internal exception-nesting detail of the external library, not an advertised stable contract. AC-2 verifies via id() identity/chain tests, but the plan does not state whether these tests drive a REAL pydantic-ai retry-exhaustion or a hand-constructed exception chain. A synthetic chain would pass green even if the real library nests differently, so the changed risky path (real exhaustion producing the wrapped exception) would never be exercised.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fca414798f9e1be77","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Acceptance Criteria line 2","norm_id":"n0861b181ea1d6236","priority":0.3972,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["pydantic-ai patch bump changes the internal exception nesting and the synthetic-chain tests stay green while production translation breaks"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add to Testing/AC-2 that the validation-exhaustion identity test triggers exhaustion through the actual Agent run against a stub model that repeatedly returns invalid output, asserting on the exception object pydantic-ai actually raises.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_